    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Drake Baldwin** (66.27) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.24) anchor the Austin Waves, representing our strongest offensive plays. **Drake Baldwin** benefits from a prime slotting in the two-hole against a favorable matchup with Brandon Pfaadt, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a high-floor start despite a mediocre order position, as he gains significant efficiency from favorable wind conditions against Robert Gasser. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Heliot Ramos** (63.54) are similarly positioned to capitalize on a soft matchup against Shane Bieber, where their platoon advantages and the pitcher\u2019s high xERA offer the best path to production in the HR and RBI categories.\n\nStrategic decisions today highlight the premium we place on matchup context over raw talent. The most difficult bench decision involved **Wade Meckler** (54.93), who barely missed the cut; while his leadoff projected status offered high volume potential, the optimizer favored the more consistent base floor and specific situational utility provided by **Nasim Nunez** and **Dominic Smith** against their respective targets. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (56.43) remains in the lineup despite a tough draw against Gerrit Cole; his elite BvP track record\u2014garnered over 41 plate appearances\u2014provided just enough of an edge to keep him in the starting nine. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly as it relates to **Gunnar Henderson** (60.09) and **Coby Mayo** (55.80). While both are currently projected to start against the slower delivery of Steven Matz, which historically boosts our stolen base ceiling, any drastic change to the batting order or a late scratch could necessitate a pivot to **Jackson Merrill** (51.51) or **Miguel Vargas** (43.96) to preserve our daily game caps. Ensure all roster locks are monitored until the official lineups clear.",
